{"cluster_id": "C-3613", "topic": "Consolidated The default `gc_fold_threshold = 1` preserves today's behavior fo", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B006-072", "B006-075", "B035-017", "B035-020"], "canonical_claim": "The default `gc_fold_threshold = 1` preserves today's behavior for changed rounds and defers only zero-delta idle rounds; `gc_fold_max_defer_rounds = 8` is inert at threshold 1 and matters when batching is enabled with a threshold greater than 1. Additionally, `PoolConfig::gc_fold_threshold` is a `uint64_t` defaulting to 1, and `PoolConfig::gc_fold_max_defer_rounds` is a `uint64_t` defaulting to 8; the pure predicate is `shouldDeferRound(size_t, bool, uint64_t, uint64_t, uint64_t)`. Additionally, The default `gc_fold_threshold` is 1, so a touched active shard is folded and trimmed each round while idle rounds can defer; the proposed production cadence is roughly `gc_interval_sec` 30\u201360 seconds with journal-pressure triggering. Additionally, The idle-GC skip-unchanged mechanism uses `gc_fold_threshold` with default 1 and bounds deferral with `gc_fold_max_defer_rounds`, default 8; `graduationDue` forces a fold before the deferral bound expires.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-06-cas-gc-round-skip-unchanged.md#L99-L110", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-06-cas-gc-round-skip-unchanged-design.md#L167-L179", "utils/ca-soak/scenarios/BACKLOG.md#L774-L801", "utils/ca-soak/scenarios/BACKLOG.md#L994-L1003"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3614", "topic": "The cache-over-CA test policy is named `cas_cache`, with CA disk `disk_ca_s3` wr", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B007-094"], "canonical_claim": "The cache-over-CA test policy is named `cas_cache`, with CA disk `disk_ca_s3` wrapped by `disk_ca_s3_cache` using `<type>cache</type>` and a one-billion-byte local cache.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-08-cas-file-cache-disk-support.md#task-1"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3615", "topic": "Consolidated The retained part-folder view cache defaults to 64 MiB, `cas_part", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B008-038", "B008-039", "B008-085", "B039-056", "B039-057", "B039-059", "B044-070"], "canonical_claim": "The retained part-folder view cache defaults to 64 MiB, `cas_part_folder_cache_max_entries` defaults to 10000, and `cas_part_folder_cache_max_entry_bytes` defaults to 16 MiB. Additionally, `cas_part_folder_cache_bytes = 0` disables retained view caching and is a supported permanent operational configuration. Additionally, The retained-view settings are `cas_part_folder_cache_bytes = 64 MiB`, `cas_part_folder_cache_max_entries = 10000`, and `cas_part_folder_cache_max_entry_bytes = 16 MiB`; zero bytes disables retention. Additionally, The suggested retained-view setting is `cas_part_folder_cache_bytes = 64 MiB`. Additionally, Setting `cas_part_folder_cache_bytes` to `0` disables retained `PartFolderView` caching without bypassing the facade. Additionally, The view cache is bounded by `cas_part_folder_cache_bytes`, `cas_part_folder_cache_max_entries`, and `cas_part_folder_cache_max_entry_bytes`. Additionally, `part_folder_cache_bytes` defaults to 64 MiB and `0` disables retention as a supported permanent operational configuration; `part_folder_cache_max_entries` defaults to 10000 and `part_folder_cache_max_entry_bytes` defaults to 16 MiB.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/en/operations/storing-data.md#L534-L539", "docs/superpowers/cas/cache.md#disabled-mode", "docs/superpowers/cas/cache.md#memory-bound", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-08-cas-part-folder-cache-phase4.md#global-constraints", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-08-cas-part-folder-cache-phase4.md#task-1", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-08-cas-part-folder-cache-design.md#cache-state-and-memory-bound"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3616", "topic": "Consolidated `manifest_decode_cache_bytes` defaults to 128 MiB and `0` disable", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B008-050", "B044-072"], "canonical_claim": "`manifest_decode_cache_bytes` defaults to 128 MiB and `0` disables manifest decode caching; the existing manifest-cache key remains `(ManifestId, Token)` so token changes force a miss and fresh decode. Additionally, `manifest_decode_cache_bytes` defaults to 128 MiB, and `0` disables decoded-manifest caching.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/en/operations/storing-data.md#L544-L545", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-08-cas-part-folder-cache-phase5.md#global-constraints"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3617", "topic": "The initial default for `ref_state_cache_bytes` is 256 MiB, and the obsolete Pha", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B010-069"], "canonical_claim": "The initial default for `ref_state_cache_bytes` is 256 MiB, and the obsolete Phase 1 design uses byte-bounded LRU caches for coherent namespace views and indexed run blocks.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-ref-snapshot-log-design.md#byte-bounded-ref-state-cache"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3618", "topic": "The initial target size for a ref-base run is `Q = 8 MiB`, and ref-base PUTs sat", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B010-076"], "canonical_claim": "The initial target size for a ref-base run is `Q = 8 MiB`, and ref-base PUTs satisfy `ref_base_puts <= ceil(S_next / Q) + 1` for `S_next` bytes in the complete next base.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-ref-snapshot-log-design.md#gc-owned-fold-format"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3619", "topic": "`snapshot_min_log_age_ms` delays snapshot coverage of young logs to reduce the l", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B011-103"], "canonical_claim": "`snapshot_min_log_age_ms` delays snapshot coverage of young logs to reduce the late-predecessor completion window, but it is a wall-clock risk reduction and not a correctness proof.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-design.md#late-predecessor-put"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3620", "topic": "Consolidated `cas_staging_backend` accepts `local` or `s3`, and `cas_s3_stagin", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B011-125", "B044-062"], "canonical_claim": "`cas_staging_backend` accepts `local` or `s3`, and `cas_s3_staging_min_bytes` defaults to approximately 64 MiB; blobs below the threshold remain on the local path and inline blobs at or below `INLINE_CAP` are unaffected. Additionally, `staging_backend` accepts `local` or `s3`; `local` is the default and stages in-flight part data locally, while `s3` enables S3-native staging.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/en/operations/storing-data.md#L509-L511", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-s3-native-staging-design.md#config"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3621", "topic": "Writable startup rejects configurations where `attempt_timeout + lease_safety_ma", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B012-020", "B012-079"], "canonical_claim": "Writable startup rejects configurations where `attempt_timeout + lease_safety_margin >= mount_lease_ttl`, and effective timeout-controller values are exposed in logs.; The initial configuration invariant is `attempt_timeout + lease_safety_margin < mount lease TTL`; the current 30-second attempt timeout with a 30-second lease TTL is rejected for protocol-significant writer operations.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-phase1.md#L208-L211", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-12-cas-s3-timeout-retry-control-rfc.md#required-timeout-model"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3622", "topic": "The current S3 defaults are a 1-second connect timeout, 30-second send/receive r", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B012-069"], "canonical_claim": "The current S3 defaults are a 1-second connect timeout, 30-second send/receive request timeout, 500 automatic retries for up to 501 HTTP attempts, a 30-second mount lease TTL, and a 10-second renewal period.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-12-cas-s3-timeout-retry-control-rfc.md#current-behavior"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3623", "topic": "CAS-specific settings include `cas_s3_connect_timeout_ms`, `cas_s3_attempt_timeo", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B012-086"], "canonical_claim": "CAS-specific settings include `cas_s3_connect_timeout_ms`, `cas_s3_attempt_timeout_ms`, `cas_s3_operation_timeout_ms`, `cas_s3_read_retry_attempts`, `cas_s3_conditional_write_retry_attempts = 0`, `cas_s3_retry_initial_backoff_ms`, `cas_s3_retry_max_backoff_ms`, and `cas_mount_lease_safety_margin_ms`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-12-cas-s3-timeout-retry-control-rfc.md#configuration"]}
