{"cluster_id": "C-3626", "topic": "Consolidated The proposed `part_folder_validate` setting has modes `always`, `", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B014-038", "B015-107", "B044-071"], "canonical_claim": "The proposed `part_folder_validate` setting has modes `always`, `age <X>`, and `never`; `always` is the current and default behavior, `age <X>` skips a body-validation `HEAD` for views validated within X seconds, and `never` removes the body re-proof while leaving `StrictValidate` callers unchanged. Additionally, The Round-B plan defines `part_folder_validate` as a string setting with `always`, `age <N>`, and `never` modes, defaulting to `always`. Additionally, `part_folder_validate` defaults to `always`, also accepts `never` or `age <seconds>`, and controls how often a `ForceFresh` read re-proves a cached manifest body with `HEAD`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/en/operations/storing-data.md#L540-L543", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-14-cas-opt-levers-s1-s5.md#task-4-3-configurable-cache-validation-part_folder_validate", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-13-cas-memory-s3-budget-optimizations-design.md#s3-validate-setting"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3627", "topic": "Consolidated Rev", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B014-062", "B014-071", "B015-007"], "canonical_claim": "Rev.6 defines the observation threshold as `mount_lease_ttl_ms + mount_lease_ttl_ms/20 + poll_interval_ms`, sets `materialization_grace_ms` to 30000 by default, uses seal id `RefTxnId{my_epoch - 1, UINT64_MAX}`, and bumps snapshot codec version 1 to 2 with `sealed_from`. Additionally, `materialization_grace_ms` is a `PoolConfig` setting with default 30000 and an XML key of the same name; an unclean or fenced mount boundary waits this grace before trusting recovery listings, while a clean boundary skips the wait. Additionally, `materialization_grace_ms` defaults to 30000 ms and is configurable.", "issue_ids": ["rev.6"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-13-cas-ref-lease-exclusivity-rev6.md#global-constraints", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-13-cas-ref-lease-exclusivity-rev6.md#task-6", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-13-cas-ref-lease-exclusivity-rev6-design.md#t-mat"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3628", "topic": "A normal reference transaction is limited by `ref_txn_max_ops = 1000`", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B017-004"], "canonical_claim": "A normal reference transaction is limited by `ref_txn_max_ops = 1000`; a transaction containing `RemoveNamespace` is a removal-class transaction subject to the 64 MiB byte budget.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-15-cas-codecs-v3-phase3-refsnaplog.md#cruxes"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3629", "topic": "The default `content_addressed_log` configuration should include `partition_by`,", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B022-068"], "canonical_claim": "The default `content_addressed_log` configuration should include `partition_by`, `max_size_rows`, `reserved_size_rows`, `buffer_size_rows_flush_threshold`, and `flush_on_crash`, while its `<ttl>` is a commented-out example.", "issue_ids": ["F8"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-21-consistency-findings-f1-f11-design.md#f8-log-config"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3630", "topic": "Consolidated The v2 ref-ledger budget uses an item cap of 1000, `ref_txn_max_o", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B023-069", "B024-016", "B024-021", "B024-079"], "canonical_claim": "The v2 ref-ledger budget uses an item cap of 1000, `ref_txn_max_ops` of 5000, and a per-operation encoded-size cap of 4 KiB; normal `ref_txn_max_bytes` is removed. Additionally, Normal ref-ledger admission uses `ref_txn_max_ops` 5000 and `kMaxRefBatch` 1000; the former byte-estimate admission and give-back spill are not used. Additionally, The normal-class whole-transaction decode cap is 20 MiB, the removal-class byte budget is 64 MiB via `ref_removal_max_bytes`, and normal-class operations have a 4 KiB per-operation cap enforced at admission and decode. Additionally, Stage-1 ref admission uses a 4096-byte per-op limit checked both during admission and decode, a 20 MiB normal-class decode cap plus writer runtime throw, and a 64 MiB `ref_removal_max_bytes` budget with no op cap for removal-class transactions.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-23-cas-writepath-stage1.md#global-constraints", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-22-cas-batched-part-commit-v2-design.md#budget", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-22-cas-writepath-stage1-internal-design.md#budget"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3631", "topic": "Consolidated The proposed per-part concurrency setting is `cas_commit_concurre", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B023-083", "B023-094", "B023-113"], "canonical_claim": "The proposed per-part concurrency setting is `cas_commit_concurrency`, with a default of 16. Additionally, `PoolConfig::cas_commit_concurrency` is planned as a `uint64` setting with default 16, while `cas_commit_pool_size` is a server setting with default 100 for the dedicated CAS commit pool. Additionally, The parallel-write implementation plan uses `cas_commit_concurrency` default 16 and a process-wide dedicated `cas_commit_pool_size` default 100, separate from the writer pool.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-22-cas-parallel-write-path.md#task-4-cas-commit-concurrency-setting-dedicated-cas-commit-pool", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-22-cas-parallel-write-path-design.md#bounded-concurrency-part-commit"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3632", "topic": "Consolidated Stage 1 adds one server-level CAS upload-pool size setting and re", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B024-026", "B024-073"], "canonical_claim": "Stage 1 adds one server-level CAS upload-pool size setting and rejects an uninitialized or zero-sized pool; non-CAS disks and engines have no behavior change. Additionally, The stage-1 pool setting `content_addressed_blob_upload_pool_size` defaults to 16, rejects 0, and the pool getter throws `LOGICAL_ERROR` before server or test initialization.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-23-cas-writepath-stage1.md#task-1", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-22-cas-writepath-stage1-internal-design.md#settings"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3633", "topic": "Consolidated The condemned-upload memory setting `content_addressed_condemned_", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B024-077", "B025-047"], "canonical_claim": "The condemned-upload memory setting `content_addressed_condemned_upload_memory_bytes` defaults to 0, meaning derived capacity of pool size multiplied by 64 MiB; the semaphore releases its permit only after `putOverwrite` returns and the body is destroyed. Additionally, The 64 MiB CAS upload value is a chosen default per-task memory budget, not a blob-body size cap; blob bodies are uncapped and an overweight body is admitted exclusively using its actual header-plus-source weight.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-23-cas-writepath-stage1.md#task-6", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-24-codex-stage1-reviews.md#round-2"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3634", "topic": "`force_owner_claim` is an opt-in per-disk setting that permits a writable open w", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B026-031"], "canonical_claim": "`force_owner_claim` is an opt-in per-disk setting that permits a writable open with a differing configured server uuid to claim the server-root as WRITE only after a mount-slot death certificate.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-25-cas-followups-detector-introspection-s42-forceclaim.md#tasks-10-12-blocked"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3635", "topic": "`write_grace_ms` is a disk-level `ContentAddressedSettings` setting with default", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B027-079"], "canonical_claim": "`write_grace_ms` is a disk-level `ContentAddressedSettings` setting with default `0`; zero disables the feature and preserves today's immediate write failure behavior.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-fence-observability-and-write-grace.md#task-3", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-28-cas-fence-observability-and-write-grace-design.md#b-setting"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3636", "topic": "Resident-snapshot incremental GC uses `gc_checkpoint_records=4096` and `gc_check", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B035-080"], "canonical_claim": "Resident-snapshot incremental GC uses `gc_checkpoint_records=4096` and `gc_checkpoint_rounds=64`; trimming is allowed only at or below the durable cursor, not merely the resident cursor.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/CONSOLIDATION-COVERAGE.md#blocking-gaps", "docs/superpowers/cas/CONSOLIDATION-COVERAGE.md#gap-fill"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3637", "topic": "The CAS configuration currently mixes `cas_scratch_path` with six `content_addre", "target": "configuration", "member_ids": ["B039-136"], "canonical_claim": "The CAS configuration currently mixes `cas_scratch_path` with six `content_addressed_*` keys: `content_addressed_gc_enabled`, `content_addressed_gc_interval_sec`, `content_addressed_root_shards`, `content_addressed_dedup_cache_bytes`, `content_addressed_dedup_head_first_min_bytes`, and `content_addressed_gc_snap_generations_to_keep`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["cas_disks_consistency_review.md#f4--config-keys-use-two-prefixes-for-one-feature-against-the-bare-key-convention"]}
